{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 (fix) — RED→GREEN landed for review as Gerrit change 2381 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2381), patch set 1.\n\nFIX (localized, 49 non-test LOC in src/rebar/review_bot/app.py): restore ADR 0067's PROCESS-level \"shutdown ≤ drain + cancel\" bound. Added a module seam `_force_process_exit(code=0)` (= `os._exit`) and `_arm_hard_shutdown(grace)` that starts a DAEMON `threading.Timer(grace, _force_process_exit)`; the lifespan `finally` arms it (`_HARD_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS = 5.0`) right after `_reconcile.clear_stop()`. Rationale: a clean teardown exits before the grace elapses (the daemon timer evaporates with the process); only a genuinely-hung orphaned `asyncio.to_thread` OS thread trips it into a hard exit — self-distinguishing on real process liveness, no fragile thread-inspection heuristic. Worst case drain+cancel+5s stays well inside the container `stop_grace_period` (1320s).\n\nRED→GREEN oracle: tests/unit/test_review_bot.py::test_shutdown_forces_process_exit_when_an_orphaned_to_thread_review_outlives_cancel drives a REAL orphaned `asyncio.to_thread(time.sleep, 1.5)` at shutdown, patches the seam to a recorder + short grace, and asserts the force-down fired.\n- Pre-fix: recorder never fires → RED (assert exits == [0] fails; asyncio.run's teardown joins the orphaned thread for the whole review).\n- Post-fix: recorder fires → GREEN.\nAsserts the force-down ACTION, not a stopwatch (dodges the banned wall-clock timing class). An autouse fixture neutralizes `_force_process_exit` to a no-op for every other lifespan test so a stale armed timer can never os._exit pytest.\n\nMUTATION (teeth): removing the `_arm_hard_shutdown(...)` call → the oracle fails RED. Restored → GREEN. 109/109 review-bot tests pass; `make lint` + `make typecheck` clean.\n\nSTEP 7 sibling sweep: only two FastAPI lifespans exist (review_bot, opcert_service). `opcert_service` already addressed the SAME class (bug c89f) via an app-owned executor it abandons on shutdown (`executor.shutdown(wait=False, cancel_futures=True)`) — NOT left with the identical defect. review-bot has ~24 `asyncio.to_thread` sites across app/voter/reconcile, so an owned-executor refactor would be large/cross-file; the localized daemon-deadline backstop restores the invariant surgically. No other uvicorn lifespan services.\n\nAttribution: caused_by → c2ba-98bf-ca2d-481a (class plan_defect): c2ba/melting-resting-serpent bounded only the asyncio await, not the process, so the ADR-0067 process-level bound was claimed but never delivered.\n\nNEXT: awaiting LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1, then Submit; ticket closed only after merge with --class=plan_defect --caused-by=c2ba-98bf-ca2d-481a."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788023620676788910,"uuid":"de7687ca-035f-4f7c-8d01-154011231d41"}